{
  "opening": "The marshmallow library is introducing new field types for IP interfaces and refining error handling for method fields. The marshmallow-jsonschema consumer must align with these updates to ensure correct schema generation and robust error reporting.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m08",
      "text": "The marshmallow library must expose the public names IPInterface, IPv4Interface, IPv6, and IPv6Interface as valid field classes that can be instantiated and used within schemas. These fields must correctly serialize and deserialize IP interface data according to their respective standards."
    },
    {
      "id": "m16",
      "text": "The marshmallow library must raise an AttributeError when a Schema class references a missing method via the Method field's name attribute. Additionally, errors raised by the callable in a Method field must be propagated during schema initialization rather than being silently caught or converted to different exception types."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please verify that these behaviors are observable through the public API before merging."
}
